<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.gascity.jsonl-hourly-offsite-age</string>

  <!-- Age alarm of the JSONL upload to S3, the leg that does NOT depend on the gc controller (2026-10-23, ga-c0939v.7).

       WHAT: runs the age check mode of packs/town-deltas/assets/scripts/jsonl-hourly-offsite.sh. It reads the LastModified of
       s3://urblink-dolt-backups/jsonl-hourly/latest.json (S3 clock) and pushes a phone alert when it is older than 75 min, absent,
       or could not be read twice in a row. Read only: head-object, no lock, nothing written to S3 or to the upload state.

       WHY A LAUNCHD JOB AND NOT ONLY AN ORDER: there is also a gc order with the same check (orders/jsonl-hourly-offsite-age.toml),
       and it goes live on merge, but an order is dispatched by the controller, and the controller is exactly what stalls.
       Measured on 2026-10-23 from the upload log (jsonl_hourly_cadence.py): no publication between 11:12Z and 14:45Z (3h33m) and
       none between 14:45Z and 17:06Z (2h20m), with no failure logged in either window, so the order was simply not dispatched.
       An alarm riding the same dispatcher is blind during that stall, which is the case it exists for.
       Same reasoning and same shape as reconciler-stall-detector: a raw launchd StartInterval job, not a gc order.

       SHARED STATE ON PURPOSE: this job and the order use the same alarm state file, so the 6 h alert throttle holds across both
       and one incident pushes one alert, not two. They can race on that file once in a long while (two reads in the same second);
       the worst case is one extra alert.

       CADENCE: StartInterval=600. A check takes about 2 s (one head-object, 60 s cap). PATH has /opt/homebrew/bin on purpose: aws,
       jq and GNU timeout live there, and without it every run would end as UNKNOWN (tool missing) and alert on the second one.
       Credentials come from ~/.aws (file based), the same ones the nightly S3 backup uses.

       INSTALLED 2026-10-23 by the Mayor (ga-c0939v.8): copied here from docs/runbooks, loaded from ~/Library/LaunchAgents with
       launchctl bootstrap, and registered in daemon-presence-watchdog.sh (DPW_CRITICAL plus a heartbeat line on the StandardOutPath
       below, limit 1500 s, above 2x the interval). The watchdog's PRESENCE-DRIFT sweep now expects this job to be loaded. -->

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/packs/town-deltas/assets/scripts/jsonl-hourly-offsite.sh</string>
    <string>--age-check</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>

  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>600</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/jsonl-hourly-offsite-age.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/jsonl-hourly-offsite-age.err</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/athos/go/bin:/Users/athos/.local/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/athos</string>
    <key>GC_CITY_PATH</key>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
